share-dialog-views-with-settings-consumers

Lane: cross

Unit: host-dialogs-with-shared-resources

ChildPatch: share-dialog-views-with-settings-consumers

Form: GitDiff

Segment: none

Purpose: Adapt native settings dialogs to the centered Control Center host with shared appearance and without a composer anchor.

Requires: none

Provides: Native text, masked-input and selection views with current editing preferences and list controls; a shared frame owns the shaded body, terminal-background footer and insets; a Control Center dialog stack owns nested completion, covered selection refresh, input and redraw scheduling over the supplied backdrop.

Boundary: Keep the ordinary BottomPane host, Escape interruption confirmation and permission shortcuts on their native input-area path. Feature consumers retain settings content, RPCs and failures. Preserve native widgets, exact input, cancellation and renderer geometry without routing Control Center state through ChatWidget.

Verification: Focused frame geometry and surface styles, masking, configured list controls, nested accept and cancel, covered selection refresh, input isolation, frame scheduling and centered rendering tests, followed by Proxy, Telegram and Control Center integration tests.

CrossGroup: control-center


